# Neo FM6 parameters (docs/specs/machines.md §5). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoFm6
# Operator and voice values use the DX7's own ranges (0-99 levels and rates, coarse 0-31, ...),
# so DX7 patches, SysEx banks and DX7 know-how carry over one to one.
namespace NeoBuzz.Fm6
class NeoFm6Machine
tracks 16
summary Six-operator FM synth in the DX7 style: 32 algorithms, DX7 ranges and envelopes, loads DX7 SysEx banks. Use it for electric pianos, bells, FM basses, brass and metallic tones.
import dx7_bank .syx | A DX7 SysEx file: a 32-voice bank or one voice. item picks the voice to play (1–32; default 1); its parameters are set.

group Algorithm
Algorithm   "Algorithm"     0 31   0    int 1                           | Which operators modulate which (the 32 DX7 algorithms)
    how Chooses which of the 32 wiring layouts decides how the six operators modulate each other and which reach the output.
    sound Different algorithms give different families of sounds, from stacked bell and organ layers to deep modulation chains for brass and basses.
Feedback    "Feedback"      0 7    0    int 0                           | Self-modulation of the feedback operator (7: near saw)
    how Sets how strongly the feedback operator modulates itself, from 0 to 7.
    sound Low values add a little brightness and edge, and high values turn the tone towards a buzzy saw and then noise.
OscSync     "Osc key sync"  0 1    1    switch                          | Operators restart their phase with each note
    how Makes the operators restart their phase with each new note.
    sound On gives the same attack every time, and off lets the phase float for a looser, more varied start.
Transpose   "Transpose"     0 48   24   int -24 st signed               | Transposes the whole voice
    how Transposes the whole voice by up to 24 semitones either way.
    sound Use it to move a patch to the register where it sounds best.

group Pitch envelope
PegR1       "PEG rate 1"    0 99   99   int 0                           | Pitch envelope rate 1 (99: fastest)
    how Sets how fast the pitch envelope moves through stage 1, from 0 to 99.
    sound Fast rates make the pitch change instantly and slow rates make it glide.
PegR2       "PEG rate 2"    0 99   99   int 0                           | Pitch envelope rate 2 (99: fastest)
    how Sets how fast the pitch envelope moves through stage 2, from 0 to 99.
    sound Fast rates make the pitch change instantly and slow rates make it glide.
PegR3       "PEG rate 3"    0 99   99   int 0                           | Pitch envelope rate 3 (99: fastest)
    how Sets how fast the pitch envelope moves through stage 3, from 0 to 99.
    sound Fast rates make the pitch change instantly and slow rates make it glide.
PegR4       "PEG rate 4"    0 99   99   int 0                           | Pitch envelope rate 4 (99: fastest)
    how Sets how fast the pitch envelope moves through stage 4, from 0 to 99.
    sound Fast rates make the pitch change instantly and slow rates make it glide.
PegL1       "PEG level 1"   0 99   50   int 0                           | Pitch envelope level 1 (50: no shift; 0/99: about −4/+4 octaves)
    how Sets the pitch the envelope reaches at stage 1, where 50 is no shift and the ends are about four octaves down or up.
    sound Moving the levels away from 50 adds pitch swoops, such as a short rise at the start of a note.
PegL2       "PEG level 2"   0 99   50   int 0                           | Pitch envelope level 2 (50: no shift; 0/99: about −4/+4 octaves)
    how Sets the pitch the envelope reaches at stage 2, where 50 is no shift and the ends are about four octaves down or up.
    sound Moving the levels away from 50 adds pitch swoops, such as a short rise at the start of a note.
PegL3       "PEG level 3"   0 99   50   int 0                           | Pitch envelope level 3 (50: no shift; 0/99: about −4/+4 octaves)
    how Sets the pitch the envelope reaches at stage 3, where 50 is no shift and the ends are about four octaves down or up.
    sound Moving the levels away from 50 adds pitch swoops, such as a short rise at the start of a note.
PegL4       "PEG level 4"   0 99   50   int 0                           | Pitch envelope level 4 (50: no shift; 0/99: about −4/+4 octaves)
    how Sets the pitch the envelope reaches at stage 4, where 50 is no shift and the ends are about four octaves down or up.
    sound Moving the levels away from 50 adds pitch swoops, such as a short rise at the start of a note.

group LFO
LfoWave     "LFO wave"      0 5    0    enum Triangle Saw_down Saw_up Square Sine S&H | LFO waveform
    how Chooses the LFO waveform: triangle, falling or rising saw, square, sine or random steps.
    sound Smooth shapes make vibrato, square makes trills, and random steps make stepped, unpredictable movement.
LfoSpeed    "LFO speed"     0 99   35   int 0                           | LFO rate (0: 0.06 Hz, 35: about 6 Hz, 99: about 24 Hz)
    how Sets the LFO speed from 0 to 99, about 0.06 Hz to 24 Hz.
    sound Low values are slow drifts and high values a fast flutter.
LfoDelay    "LFO delay"     0 99   0    int 0                           | Time before the LFO fades in after a note
    how Sets how long after a note the LFO takes to fade in, from 0 to 99.
    sound A delay lets the note start steady and add vibrato later, as a singer would.
LfoPmd      "LFO pitch"     0 99   0    int 0                           | Pitch modulation depth (scaled by Pitch sens)
    how Sets how deeply the LFO modulates pitch, from 0 to 99.
    sound More depth gives a stronger vibrato.
LfoAmd      "LFO amp"       0 99   0    int 0                           | Amplitude modulation depth (scaled by each operator's Amp sens)
    how Sets how deeply the LFO modulates amplitude, from 0 to 99.
    sound More depth gives a stronger tremolo on the operators that respond to it.
LfoSync     "LFO key sync"  0 1    1    switch                          | The LFO restarts with each note
    how Makes the LFO restart with each note.
    sound On gives every note the same vibrato start, and off lets the LFO run freely.
PitchSens   "Pitch sens"    0 7    3    int 0                           | How far LFO, mod wheel and aftertouch move the pitch
    how Sets how far the LFO, mod wheel and aftertouch can move the pitch, from 0 to 7.
    sound Low values keep vibrato subtle and high values make it wide.

group Voice
VoiceMode   "Voice mode"    0 2    0    enum Poly Mono Legato           | Poly; Mono retriggers; Legato glides without retriggering
    how Chooses how notes share voices: Poly plays chords, Mono retriggers on each note, Legato glides between overlapping notes.
    sound Poly suits keys and pads, Mono gives a punchy lead or bass, and Legato gives smooth, connected lines.
Polyphony   "Polyphony"     1 16   8    int 0                           | Notes that sound at once
    how Sets how many notes can sound at once, from 1 to 16.
    sound More voices let chords and long releases overlap, and fewer save processing power.
Unison      "Unison"        1 4    1    int 0                           | Voices per note
    how Sets the number of stacked voices per note, from 1 to 4.
    sound More voices make the note thicker and wider, and one voice is a single clean tone.
UniDetune   "Uni detune"    0 1000 150  pct                             | Detune between unison voices (up to ±25 cents)
    how Sets how far apart the unison voices are tuned, up to 25 cents.
    sound Small amounts give a warm thickness and large ones a wide chorus-like swarm.
UniSpread   "Uni spread"    0 1000 600  pct                             | Stereo spread of unison voices
    how Sets how widely the unison voices are spread across the stereo field, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound More spread makes the note wider, and zero keeps it centred.
GlideMode   "Glide mode"    0 2    0    enum Off Always Legato          | When notes glide
    how Chooses when notes slide into each other: never, always, or only on overlapping notes.
    sound Gliding adds a singing slur between notes.
Glide       "Glide"         0 1000 200  pow 0 2 3 s 3                   | Glide time
    how Sets how long the slide takes, up to 2 seconds.
    sound Short glides are subtle and long ones sweep slowly between pitches.
BendRange   "Bend range"    0 12   2    int 0 st                        | Pitch bend range
    how Sets how far the pitch bend wheel moves the pitch, from 0 to 12 semitones.
    sound A small range gives expressive nudges and a large one gives big sweeps.

group Controllers
WheelPitch  "Wheel pitch"   0 99   50   int 0                           | Mod wheel → pitch modulation (vibrato from the LFO)
    how Sets how much the mod wheel adds LFO vibrato, from 0 to 99.
    sound Pushing the wheel up brings in vibrato, which makes held notes feel more expressive.
WheelAmp    "Wheel amp"     0 99   0    int 0                           | Mod wheel → amplitude modulation
    how Sets how much the mod wheel adds LFO tremolo, from 0 to 99.
    sound Pushing the wheel up brings in a pulsing volume change.
AtPitch     "AT pitch"      0 99   0    int 0                           | Aftertouch → pitch modulation
    how Sets how much key pressure after the note starts adds LFO vibrato, from 0 to 99.
    sound Pressing harder on a held key adds vibrato.
AtAmp       "AT amp"        0 99   0    int 0                           | Aftertouch → amplitude modulation
    how Sets how much key pressure after the note starts adds LFO tremolo, from 0 to 99.
    sound Pressing harder on a held key adds a pulsing volume change.

group Output
Tone        "Tone"          0 1000 1000 freq 1000 20000                 | Gentle low-pass on the output (20 kHz: open)
    how Applies a gentle low-pass filter to the output, from 1 to 20 kHz.
    sound Lowering it takes the edge off the top, and fully open it leaves the sound unfiltered.
EngineMode  "Engine"        0 1    0    enum Clean_2× Raw_1×             | Clean: 2× oversampled; Raw: the original's aliasing grit
    how Chooses Clean (oversampled twice) or Raw (no oversampling).
    sound Clean is smooth and quiet at the top, and Raw keeps the gritty aliasing of the classic hardware sound.
Volume      "Volume"        0 1000 739  db -40 6 inf                    | Output level
    how Sets the output level of the synth, from -40 to +6 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to place the instrument in the mix without changing its tone.

group Operator 1
O1On      "Op1 on"       0 1    1    switch                          | Operator 1 sounds (off: silent, as on the DX7)
    how Turns operator 1 on or off.
    sound Muting one operator shows what it adds to the sound.
O1Level   "Op1 level"    0 99   99   int 0                           | Output level (carriers: loudness; modulators: brightness)
    how Sets the output level of operator 1, from 0 to 99.
    sound For a carrier this is loudness, and for a modulator it is brightness: more level makes a harsher, richer tone.
O1Mode    "Op1 mode"     0 1    0    enum Ratio Fixed                | Ratio: follows the note; Fixed: a fixed frequency
    how Chooses whether operator 1 follows the note pitch or runs at a fixed frequency.
    sound Ratio mode plays in tune across the keyboard, and Fixed mode gives a constant tone for noise-like or percussive effects.
O1Coarse  "Op1 coarse"   0 31   1    int 0                           | Ratio 0.5, 1 … 31 (Fixed: 1, 10, 100, 1000 Hz)
    how Sets the frequency ratio of operator 1 in whole steps, from 0.5 to 31.
    sound Whole-number ratios give harmonic tones and others give bells and metallic sounds.
O1Fine    "Op1 fine"     0 99   0    int 0                           | Ratio +0 … +99% (Fixed: ×1 … ×9.77)
    how Adds a fine amount to the frequency ratio of operator 1, from 0 to 99 %.
    sound Small offsets detune the operator for a slow beating, and larger ones give inharmonic colour.
O1Detune  "Op1 detune"   0 14   7    int -7 signed                   | Detune, −7 … +7 (about 1 cent a step at A4)
    how Detunes operator 1 by about 7 cents either way.
    sound A little detune adds a gentle movement against the other operators.
O1Wave    "Op1 wave"     0 3    0    enum Sine Half_sine Abs_sine Pulse_sine | Operator waveform (Sine: DX7)
    how Chooses the waveform of operator 1: sine, half sine, absolute sine or pulse sine.
    sound Sine is the classic tone, and the other shapes add more harmonics and a harsher edge.
O1R1      "Op1 rate 1"   0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope rate 1 (99: fastest)
    how Sets how fast the envelope of operator 1 moves through stage 1, from 0 to 99.
    sound Fast rates make instant changes, and slow rates make the level glide over time.
O1R2      "Op1 rate 2"   0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope rate 2 (99: fastest)
    how Sets how fast the envelope of operator 1 moves through stage 2, from 0 to 99.
    sound Fast rates make instant changes, and slow rates make the level glide over time.
O1R3      "Op1 rate 3"   0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope rate 3 (99: fastest)
    how Sets how fast the envelope of operator 1 moves through stage 3, from 0 to 99.
    sound Fast rates make instant changes, and slow rates make the level glide over time.
O1R4      "Op1 rate 4"   0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope rate 4 (99: fastest)
    how Sets how fast the envelope of operator 1 moves through stage 4, from 0 to 99.
    sound Fast rates make instant changes, and slow rates make the level glide over time.
O1L1      "Op1 level 1"  0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope level 1
    how Sets the level of the envelope of operator 1 at stage 1, from 0 to 99.
    sound Together the four levels shape how the operator swells, decays and fades away.
O1L2      "Op1 level 2"  0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope level 2
    how Sets the level of the envelope of operator 1 at stage 2, from 0 to 99.
    sound Together the four levels shape how the operator swells, decays and fades away.
O1L3      "Op1 level 3"  0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope level 3
    how Sets the level of the envelope of operator 1 at stage 3, from 0 to 99.
    sound Together the four levels shape how the operator swells, decays and fades away.
O1L4      "Op1 level 4"  0 99   0    int 0                           | Envelope level 4
    how Sets the level of the envelope of operator 1 at stage 4, from 0 to 99.
    sound Together the four levels shape how the operator swells, decays and fades away.
O1Break   "Op1 break"    0 99   39   int 0                           | Keyboard scaling break point (39: C4)
    how Sets the key at which level scaling for operator 1 changes sides, from 0 to 99, where 39 is middle C.
    sound Notes either side of the break point are scaled by the depth settings.
O1LDepth  "Op1 L depth"  0 99   0    int 0                           | Level scaling below the break point
    how Sets how much the level of operator 1 changes for keys below the break point, from 0 to 99.
    sound It lets low notes sound brighter or softer than the middle of the keyboard.
O1RDepth  "Op1 R depth"  0 99   0    int 0                           | Level scaling above the break point
    how Sets how much the level of operator 1 changes for keys above the break point, from 0 to 99.
    sound It lets high notes sound brighter or softer than the middle of the keyboard.
O1LCurve  "Op1 L curve"  0 3    0    enum -Lin -Exp +Exp +Lin        | Scaling curve below the break point
    how Chooses the shape of the level scaling below the break point: linear or exponential, falling or rising.
    sound Exponential curves change faster near the extremes, linear curves change evenly.
O1RCurve  "Op1 R curve"  0 3    0    enum -Lin -Exp +Exp +Lin        | Scaling curve above the break point
    how Chooses the shape of the level scaling above the break point: linear or exponential, falling or rising.
    sound Exponential curves change faster near the extremes, linear curves change evenly.
O1RateSc  "Op1 rate sc"  0 7    0    int 0                           | Envelopes run faster for higher notes
    how Makes the envelope of operator 1 run faster for higher notes, from 0 to 7.
    sound Higher notes decay sooner, as they do on a plucked or struck instrument.
O1AmpSens "Op1 amp sens" 0 3    0    int 0                           | How much LFO / wheel / aftertouch amplitude modulation applies
    how Sets how much LFO, wheel and aftertouch amplitude modulation reaches operator 1, from 0 to 3.
    sound Higher values let tremolo shape this operator, and zero leaves it steady.
O1VelSens "Op1 vel sens" 0 7    0    int 0                           | How much velocity changes the level
    how Sets how much note velocity changes the level of operator 1, from 0 to 7.
    sound Higher values make hard playing brighter or louder, depending on whether it is a modulator or a carrier.

group Operator 2
O2On      "Op2 on"       0 1    1    switch                          | Operator 2 sounds (off: silent, as on the DX7)
    how Turns operator 2 on or off.
    sound Muting one operator shows what it adds to the sound.
O2Level   "Op2 level"    0 99   0    int 0                           | Output level (carriers: loudness; modulators: brightness)
    how Sets the output level of operator 2, from 0 to 99.
    sound For a carrier this is loudness, and for a modulator it is brightness: more level makes a harsher, richer tone.
O2Mode    "Op2 mode"     0 1    0    enum Ratio Fixed                | Ratio: follows the note; Fixed: a fixed frequency
    how Chooses whether operator 2 follows the note pitch or runs at a fixed frequency.
    sound Ratio mode plays in tune across the keyboard, and Fixed mode gives a constant tone for noise-like or percussive effects.
O2Coarse  "Op2 coarse"   0 31   1    int 0                           | Ratio 0.5, 1 … 31 (Fixed: 1, 10, 100, 1000 Hz)
    how Sets the frequency ratio of operator 2 in whole steps, from 0.5 to 31.
    sound Whole-number ratios give harmonic tones and others give bells and metallic sounds.
O2Fine    "Op2 fine"     0 99   0    int 0                           | Ratio +0 … +99% (Fixed: ×1 … ×9.77)
    how Adds a fine amount to the frequency ratio of operator 2, from 0 to 99 %.
    sound Small offsets detune the operator for a slow beating, and larger ones give inharmonic colour.
O2Detune  "Op2 detune"   0 14   7    int -7 signed                   | Detune, −7 … +7 (about 1 cent a step at A4)
    how Detunes operator 2 by about 7 cents either way.
    sound A little detune adds a gentle movement against the other operators.
O2Wave    "Op2 wave"     0 3    0    enum Sine Half_sine Abs_sine Pulse_sine | Operator waveform (Sine: DX7)
    how Chooses the waveform of operator 2: sine, half sine, absolute sine or pulse sine.
    sound Sine is the classic tone, and the other shapes add more harmonics and a harsher edge.
O2R1      "Op2 rate 1"   0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope rate 1 (99: fastest)
    how Sets how fast the envelope of operator 2 moves through stage 1, from 0 to 99.
    sound Fast rates make instant changes, and slow rates make the level glide over time.
O2R2      "Op2 rate 2"   0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope rate 2 (99: fastest)
    how Sets how fast the envelope of operator 2 moves through stage 2, from 0 to 99.
    sound Fast rates make instant changes, and slow rates make the level glide over time.
O2R3      "Op2 rate 3"   0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope rate 3 (99: fastest)
    how Sets how fast the envelope of operator 2 moves through stage 3, from 0 to 99.
    sound Fast rates make instant changes, and slow rates make the level glide over time.
O2R4      "Op2 rate 4"   0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope rate 4 (99: fastest)
    how Sets how fast the envelope of operator 2 moves through stage 4, from 0 to 99.
    sound Fast rates make instant changes, and slow rates make the level glide over time.
O2L1      "Op2 level 1"  0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope level 1
    how Sets the level of the envelope of operator 2 at stage 1, from 0 to 99.
    sound Together the four levels shape how the operator swells, decays and fades away.
O2L2      "Op2 level 2"  0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope level 2
    how Sets the level of the envelope of operator 2 at stage 2, from 0 to 99.
    sound Together the four levels shape how the operator swells, decays and fades away.
O2L3      "Op2 level 3"  0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope level 3
    how Sets the level of the envelope of operator 2 at stage 3, from 0 to 99.
    sound Together the four levels shape how the operator swells, decays and fades away.
O2L4      "Op2 level 4"  0 99   0    int 0                           | Envelope level 4
    how Sets the level of the envelope of operator 2 at stage 4, from 0 to 99.
    sound Together the four levels shape how the operator swells, decays and fades away.
O2Break   "Op2 break"    0 99   39   int 0                           | Keyboard scaling break point (39: C4)
    how Sets the key at which level scaling for operator 2 changes sides, from 0 to 99, where 39 is middle C.
    sound Notes either side of the break point are scaled by the depth settings.
O2LDepth  "Op2 L depth"  0 99   0    int 0                           | Level scaling below the break point
    how Sets how much the level of operator 2 changes for keys below the break point, from 0 to 99.
    sound It lets low notes sound brighter or softer than the middle of the keyboard.
O2RDepth  "Op2 R depth"  0 99   0    int 0                           | Level scaling above the break point
    how Sets how much the level of operator 2 changes for keys above the break point, from 0 to 99.
    sound It lets high notes sound brighter or softer than the middle of the keyboard.
O2LCurve  "Op2 L curve"  0 3    0    enum -Lin -Exp +Exp +Lin        | Scaling curve below the break point
    how Chooses the shape of the level scaling below the break point: linear or exponential, falling or rising.
    sound Exponential curves change faster near the extremes, linear curves change evenly.
O2RCurve  "Op2 R curve"  0 3    0    enum -Lin -Exp +Exp +Lin        | Scaling curve above the break point
    how Chooses the shape of the level scaling above the break point: linear or exponential, falling or rising.
    sound Exponential curves change faster near the extremes, linear curves change evenly.
O2RateSc  "Op2 rate sc"  0 7    0    int 0                           | Envelopes run faster for higher notes
    how Makes the envelope of operator 2 run faster for higher notes, from 0 to 7.
    sound Higher notes decay sooner, as they do on a plucked or struck instrument.
O2AmpSens "Op2 amp sens" 0 3    0    int 0                           | How much LFO / wheel / aftertouch amplitude modulation applies
    how Sets how much LFO, wheel and aftertouch amplitude modulation reaches operator 2, from 0 to 3.
    sound Higher values let tremolo shape this operator, and zero leaves it steady.
O2VelSens "Op2 vel sens" 0 7    0    int 0                           | How much velocity changes the level
    how Sets how much note velocity changes the level of operator 2, from 0 to 7.
    sound Higher values make hard playing brighter or louder, depending on whether it is a modulator or a carrier.

group Operator 3
