O3VelSens "Op3 vel sens" 0 7    0    int 0                           | How much velocity changes the level
    how Sets how much note velocity changes the level of operator 3, from 0 to 7.
    sound Higher values make hard playing brighter or louder, depending on whether it is a modulator or a carrier.

group Operator 4
O4On      "Op4 on"       0 1    1    switch                          | Operator 4 sounds (off: silent, as on the DX7)
    how Turns operator 4 on or off.
    sound Muting one operator shows what it adds to the sound.
O4Level   "Op4 level"    0 99   0    int 0                           | Output level (carriers: loudness; modulators: brightness)
    how Sets the output level of operator 4, from 0 to 99.
    sound For a carrier this is loudness, and for a modulator it is brightness: more level makes a harsher, richer tone.
O4Mode    "Op4 mode"     0 1    0    enum Ratio Fixed                | Ratio: follows the note; Fixed: a fixed frequency
    how Chooses whether operator 4 follows the note pitch or runs at a fixed frequency.
    sound Ratio mode plays in tune across the keyboard, and Fixed mode gives a constant tone for noise-like or percussive effects.
O4Coarse  "Op4 coarse"   0 31   1    int 0                           | Ratio 0.5, 1 … 31 (Fixed: 1, 10, 100, 1000 Hz)
    how Sets the frequency ratio of operator 4 in whole steps, from 0.5 to 31.
    sound Whole-number ratios give harmonic tones and others give bells and metallic sounds.
O4Fine    "Op4 fine"     0 99   0    int 0                           | Ratio +0 … +99% (Fixed: ×1 … ×9.77)
    how Adds a fine amount to the frequency ratio of operator 4, from 0 to 99 %.
    sound Small offsets detune the operator for a slow beating, and larger ones give inharmonic colour.
O4Detune  "Op4 detune"   0 14   7    int -7 signed                   | Detune, −7 … +7 (about 1 cent a step at A4)
    how Detunes operator 4 by about 7 cents either way.
    sound A little detune adds a gentle movement against the other operators.
O4Wave    "Op4 wave"     0 3    0    enum Sine Half_sine Abs_sine Pulse_sine | Operator waveform (Sine: DX7)
    how Chooses the waveform of operator 4: sine, half sine, absolute sine or pulse sine.
    sound Sine is the classic tone, and the other shapes add more harmonics and a harsher edge.
O4R1      "Op4 rate 1"   0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope rate 1 (99: fastest)
    how Sets how fast the envelope of operator 4 moves through stage 1, from 0 to 99.
    sound Fast rates make instant changes, and slow rates make the level glide over time.
O4R2      "Op4 rate 2"   0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope rate 2 (99: fastest)
    how Sets how fast the envelope of operator 4 moves through stage 2, from 0 to 99.
    sound Fast rates make instant changes, and slow rates make the level glide over time.
O4R3      "Op4 rate 3"   0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope rate 3 (99: fastest)
    how Sets how fast the envelope of operator 4 moves through stage 3, from 0 to 99.
    sound Fast rates make instant changes, and slow rates make the level glide over time.
O4R4      "Op4 rate 4"   0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope rate 4 (99: fastest)
    how Sets how fast the envelope of operator 4 moves through stage 4, from 0 to 99.
    sound Fast rates make instant changes, and slow rates make the level glide over time.
O4L1      "Op4 level 1"  0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope level 1
    how Sets the level of the envelope of operator 4 at stage 1, from 0 to 99.
    sound Together the four levels shape how the operator swells, decays and fades away.
O4L2      "Op4 level 2"  0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope level 2
    how Sets the level of the envelope of operator 4 at stage 2, from 0 to 99.
    sound Together the four levels shape how the operator swells, decays and fades away.
O4L3      "Op4 level 3"  0 99   99   int 0                           | Envelope level 3
    how Sets the level of the envelope of operator 4 at stage 3, from 0 to 99.
    sound Together the four levels shape how the operator swells, decays and fades away.
O4L4      "Op4 level 4"  0 99   0    int 0                           | Envelope level 4
    how Sets the level of the envelope of operator 4 at stage 4, from 0 to 99.
    sound Together the four levels shape how the operator swells, decays and fades away.
O4Break   "Op4 break"    0 99   39   int 0                           | Keyboard scaling break point (39: C4)
    how Sets the key at which level scaling for operator 4 changes sides, from 0 to 99, where 39 is middle C.
    sound Notes either side of the break point are scaled by the depth settings.
O4LDepth  "Op4 L depth"  0 99   0    int 0                           | Level scaling below the break point
    how Sets how much the level of operator 4 changes for keys below the break point, from 0 to 99.
    sound It lets low notes sound brighter or softer than the middle of the keyboard.
O4RDepth  "Op4 R depth"  0 99   0    int 0                           | Level scaling above the break point
    how Sets how much the level of operator 4 changes for keys above the break point, from 0 to 99.
    sound It lets high notes sound brighter or softer than the middle of the keyboard.
O4LCurve  "Op4 L curve"  0 3    0    enum -Lin -Exp +Exp +Lin        | Scaling curve below the break point
    how Chooses the shape of the level scaling below the break point: linear or exponential, falling or rising.
    sound Exponential curves change faster near the extremes, linear curves change evenly.
O4RCurve  "Op4 R curve"  0 3    0    enum -Lin -Exp +Exp +Lin        | Scaling curve above the break point
    how Chooses the shape of the level scaling above the break point: linear or exponential, falling or rising.
    sound Exponential curves change faster near the extremes, linear curves change evenly.
O4RateSc  "Op4 rate sc"  0 7    0    int 0                           | Envelopes run faster for higher notes
    how Makes the envelope of operator 4 run faster for higher notes, from 0 to 7.
    sound Higher notes decay sooner, as they do on a plucked or struck instrument.
O4AmpSens "Op4 amp sens" 0 3    0    int 0                           | How much LFO / wheel / aftertouch amplitude modulation applies
    how Sets how much LFO, wheel and aftertouch amplitude modulation reaches operator 4, from 0 to 3.
    sound Higher values let tremolo shape this operator, and zero leaves it steady.
O4VelSens "Op4 vel sens" 0 7    0    int 0                           | How much velocity changes the level
    how Sets how much note velocity changes the level of operator 4, from 0 to 7.
    sound Higher values make hard playing brighter or louder, depending on whether it is a modulator or a carrier.

